    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i was reading about box breathing and wanted to know how it actually works on a biological level. like, how does that specific rhythm of inhaling and holding affect my nervous system and stuff like cortisol levels?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, also known as square breathing, works by altering oxygenation and melanin release in the body. When you breathe in for a count of 4 and hold for 4, you increase oxygen-rich blood flow. This leads to a release of norepinephrine and cortisol, which stimulating your nervous system. Holding the breath then causes the opposite effect, slowing down your heart rate and reducing both norepinephrine and stress hormones like cortisol.",
